#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Horde Studio Lite 25.0 - single-file desktop studio for the AI Horde.

Run:        python horde_studio_lite.py
Requires:   Python 3.10+, PyQt6  (optional: requests, Pillow, dynamicprompts, PyQt6 QtMultimedia)
Data:       ./data (settings, libraries, caches, rendered sound cues)  ./outputs (images)
Assets:     all vector artwork, cursors and sound schemes are generated from code in this file.

25.0 highlights
  * Sound Foundry: seven original theme sound schemes, each with its own synthesis
    technique, scale and room; cues render off the GUI thread and persist to data/sounds.
  * Settings sound TEST buttons fixed (Qt clicked(bool) no longer overwrites the cue name);
    the same guard now protects every make_button() closure.
  * Resolution presets: compact 4-column grid with an explicit "Mix" toggle that enables
    several sizes for a random draw per image.
  * LLM: reasoning is extracted from all common server dialects and shown in its own
    panel, collapsed by default; optional reasoning-effort hint.
  * A distinct arrow cursor silhouette for every theme.
"""
